# Piece 4 proposed route

Read-only plan. Implement only after the piece 3 PR is open. The diagnosis is in `piece4-diagnosis.md`; no geometry or test changes have been made for this piece.

Start with five source jobs: worker LOD2, woman-shawl LOD1/2, gaucho LOD1/2. Keep all close models exact. Correct the visible defects first. Add no new seam, tube, strap or fastener in this pass.

| Owner | Proposed files | Boundary |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Geometry author | New `assets/source/characters-3d/authoring/coarse_garment_surfaces.py`; narrow hook in `optimize.py`; source-job facts hook in `build.py` if needed | Deferred vest/shawl shell construction and coarse poncho normals only. Keep material inventory/order, atlas authoring and all original colour recipes exact. |
| Bounded export installer | New `tools/characters-3d/build-coarse-garment-surfaces.py`; selected-job integration in `build-library.py` | Build five fresh source outputs privately. Verify them, graft only their allowed outfit data onto exact retained native bodies, replay the existing source passes, then install only those five bodies and owned record changes. |
| Verification author | New `tests/characters-coarse-garment-surfaces.test.mjs`; source fixture/proposal helper as needed; narrow lineage integration in existing pilot/family/apparel and pipeline tests | Keep historical source/hash anchors. Add explicit proof of the approved native correction rather than replacing old golden hashes. Keep existing rig, motion, hem, boot and strict donor checks. |
| Root | Review fixture/UI only if needed; plan/visual record and PR | Review 44/88 px, relevant views/actions, measured triangle/draw/bounds changes, and gates. |

The smallest geometry hook separates reduction from atlas packing. Defer only the target vest/shawl object, reduce the coat through the unchanged LOD settings, then build its overlay from the final coat triangles. Use the current region predicates and original garment material. Copy the exact four normalized weights from each corresponding coat vertex. Keep the original 3 mm vest and 9 mm shawl offsets as the initial fit; apply only the smallest bounded outward adjustment required by the clearance gate. Do not decimate the derived shell again. Keep the old material slot in the source inventory so its pigment tile and normal/roughness resources remain stable.

For gaucho LOD1/2, set geometric face shading on the poncho object after reduction and before joining/export. Keep LOD0 smooth. A glTF exporter may duplicate vertices for separate corner normals; prove identical oriented triangles, positions, UVs, colours and skin weights. No added triangles or draw calls are allowed. Do not change the normal map or pigment to hide the defect.

Use the new source output as the geometry donor, not as an unrestricted whole-body replacement. Verify matching rigs and material resources; retain every unowned part and all rig/socket data from the released native body. If the exported material/UV roles differ, reject the candidate rather than silently changing old maps. Retain a compact source receipt with the old body/record hashes and exact reversible owned replacements. This preserves the old baseline anchor while allowing the new approved native geometry below frozen colour stages.

The private replay order is: verified apparel unwind; verified pilot/family unwind to the native inputs; selected source correction; long-cloth support and close boot support; reviewed coarse topology; shawl palette; UV1 hem; final coarse topology; unchanged pilot and family recipes; unchanged apparel recipe. Require strict final apparel donor hashes and strict lower family donor hashes on a verified unwrapped view. Banks, equipment, close bodies and every other appearance/LOD remain exact. Completed replay must write zero files; fresh replay may write only the five selected bodies and their records/maps, with no bank jobs.

Geometry gates must test triangle interiors and edges, not only shared vertices. Require matched shell/coat topology and weights, positive local clearance, no target intersections, and a bounded silhouette change. Test rest plus supported idle, walk, rifle aim, `stand.gesture.throw`, crouch, prone and mounted idle at stable and transition samples. For the poncho, require each corner normal to agree with its panel face and no averaging across opposing shell sides. Compare the untouched triangles/parts and full material/UV roles exactly.

Budget: worker LOD2 has no triangle growth; shawl LOD1 at most +128 and LOD2 at most +144; gaucho adds zero triangles; all five add zero draws. These are rejection caps, not promises of final counts. Review front/side/rear at 44 px and 88 px before selecting any further detail. Only if a missing closure remains visible at 44 px, consider one fitted 6-triangle strip or an 8-triangle rear seam in a later bounded step, with a 48-triangle per-body cap. Do not restore the full fine seam tubes.
